You're using PC NetHack, or is that a suggestion?  Under MSDOSCOLOR
(which I'm fixing and enhancing now) the '@' symbol, no matter what it
represents on the map, should be hilited.  Of course, if you use the
graphics option to set sinks or something to the '@' symbol, this is
wrong.  Also, in 2.3, spaces are hilited, worm tails aren't, and
under some circumstances, it changes the background instead of the
foreground.  (3.0 will be more colorful, in any case.)


